/-!
E-stage exact-coefficient completion layer.

This layer keeps the analytic theorems named and explicit.  Finite checks,
including the reference Kloosterman residue sum, are represented by concrete
finite certificates; Kuznetsov, Weil-bound, and central L-value theory enter
only as named proof fields.
-/

inductive ExactCoefficientERequirement where
  | coefficientSeparationBoundary
  | thetaCoefficientFiniteCertificate
  | inducedCharacterFiniteCertificate
  | spectralKloostermanExpansionCertificate
  | localEulerDecompositionCertificate
  | rootNumberFilterCertificate
  | exactCoefficientLValueBoundary
  | paperThetaCoefficientTable
  | paperSpectralKloostermanData
  | paperLocalEulerRootNumberLValueInput
  | namedAnalyticBoundary
  | finiteResidueKloostermanSum
deriving DecidableEq, Repr

