Exact finite term data for the raw page-8 unary-theta expression.

Writing `nu = k + 1/2`, the exponential has q-exponent `nu^2 / 2`.
At characteristic `b = 0`, the involution `k |-> -k-1` preserves that
exponent and negates the coefficient `nu`.  Thus every symmetric finite
window cancels pairwise.  No nonzero analytic shadow is inferred from this
raw formula; a corrected characteristic or multiplier normalization remains
part of the analytic proof boundary.
-/

