/-!
Paper Item 1 kernel, multiplier, and cusp audit.

The finite data on pages 64-66 use the odd modulus-four character, target
multipliers `(1,1)`, `alpha = -1`, `beta = 1`, and three cusps.  These values
are represented exactly below.  Two independent consistency checks are kept
explicit:

* the displayed character has `psi(-1) = -1`, while the quoted `nu = 0`
  theta hypothesis requires parity `+1`;
* the displayed near-zero power is `-3/2`, whereas the power criterion for
  `integral_0^y0 y^p dy` is `p > -1`.

Consequently the numerical residuals are diagnostic inputs and the global
cusp-convergence statement remains an analytic boundary.
-/

