Concrete finite inside/outside data for Ramanujan's third-order mock theta.

Page 17 defines `S = 2 * psi - f(q^(-1))`; that dictionary is algebraic by
definition.  Page 25 separately gives an explicit correction series

`S(q) = (sum_n (-1)^n q^(n(n+1)/2)) / (-q; q)_infinity^2`.

The nontrivial finite check below computes both corrections independently.
It certifies their first sixteen coefficients exactly over `Int`.  The global
analytic continuation identifying the T2 object `G` with this outside series
remains an analytic proof boundary.
-/

